---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { render, legal, byName } from "../lib/md";
import { BUILDS, LAYERS } from "../data/firmware";
import { site } from "../config";
const warning = render(byName(legal, "firmware-warning.md")).html;
---
<Base title="Firmware" description="The FX Unleashed wheel app: what each build changes, how it was checked, where to download it, and how to go back to stock.">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Firmware</p>
    <h1>The <span class="red">wheel app</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Unleashed mode needs a modified version of the FX Pro's own app. What it is, where to get it, how to go back.</p>

    <div class="warning prose" role="note" id="risks">
      <p class="eyebrow">Read this first</p>
      <Fragment set:html={warning} />
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal" id="get-it">Get it</h2>
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <p><strong>Build 9</strong> (it includes builds 4 to 8) is a single file, <code>FXUnleashed-wheelapp-build9.sfu</code>: 96,272 bytes, SHA-256 <code>85E7110BA368495120C7E84D210C194D5E9EEC9EACEB3F8F7C148F020FE0F458</code>. Check the checksum before you use it.</p>
      <p class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href={site.firmwareReleases}>Download build 9</a> <a class="btn" href="/start/#1-install-the-wheel-app">Install steps</a> <a class="btn" href={site.firmwareRepo}>Repository</a></p>
      <p><strong>What it is.</strong> Simagic's own wheel app 1.3.11 with our changes. It is Simagic's software, shared by a community project without Simagic's involvement, and it may be taken down. We don't publish the key that protects Simagic's firmware, anywhere.</p>
      <p><strong>Rather make it yourself?</strong> The same repository has a patch tool that checks your own SimPro copy is Simagic's original, applies our changes and checks the result against the same checksum. You get identical bytes. Either way you install through SimPro, exactly as you would a firmware update, and then put Simagic's original back.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal" id="back-to-stock">Back to stock</h2>
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <ol>
        <li>Check SimPro's copy of the wheel app is Simagic's original (after installing the modified one you put the original back, so it is).</li>
        <li>Wheel on USB, base on. In SimPro: Device, FX Pro, Firmware: reinstall wheel app 1.3.11.</li>
        <li>Wait until SimPro says it's done. If it hangs after the wheel enters boot mode, close SimPro, start it again and reinstall: it installs to a wheel that's already in boot mode.</li>
        <li>That's Simagic's own firmware again. The plugin's Wheel tab shows no patch build.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal">What each build changes</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      {BUILDS.map(b => (
        <div class={`build reveal ${b.status}`}>
          <span class="n">{b.n}</span>
          <div><h3>{b.title} <span class="st">{b.status}</span></h3><p>{b.text}</p></div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal">How every build is checked</h2>
    <ol class="layers">
      {LAYERS.map((l, i) => (
        <li class="reveal" style={`--i:${i}`}>
          <span class="ring" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div><h3>{l.title}</h3><p>{l.text}</p></div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .page { padding: 150px 0 100px; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .warning { margin: 40px 0 80px; padding: 28px 30px; border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 176, 0, 0.35); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,176,0,0.07), rgba(255,176,0,0.02)); max-width: none; }
  .warning :global(p), .warning :global(li) { color: var(--text); }
  .warning .eyebrow { color: var(--amber); }
  .warning .eyebrow::before { background: var(--amber); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--amber); }
  h2 { margin-top: 80px; }
  .layers { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 30px 0; display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(360px, 100%), 1fr)); counter-reset: l; }
  .layers li { display: flex; gap: 18px; padding: 22px; border-radius: 18px; background: var(--panel-solid); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ring { flex: none; width: 46px; height: 46px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--red); box-shadow: 0 0 20px var(--red-glow), inset 0 0 12px var(--red-glow); position: relative; }
  .ring::after { counter-increment: l; content: counter(l); position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 700 18px var(--display); }
  .layers h3 { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .layers p { margin: 0; }
  .timeline { position: relative; margin: 30px 0; padding-left: 30px; border-left: 2px solid var(--line); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .build { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: flex-start; position: relative; }
  .build::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: -38px; top: 14px; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--green); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--green); }
  .build.next::before { background: var(--amber); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--amber); }
  .n { font: 700 44px/1 var(--display); color: var(--red); min-width: 50px; }
  .st { font: 700 10px/1 var(--display); letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: rgba(33,224,122,0.12); color: var(--green); vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 8px; }
  .next .st { background: rgba(255,176,0,0.12); color: var(--amber); }
</style>
